'' A LINUX SHARED LIBRARY is fbc's measured link, not the COFF one. 'fbc -dll -v' on
'' Linux: clang gets -fPIC, ld gets '-shared -h<basename>', and nothing is written
'' beside the .so. This build used to hand GNU ld the COFF spellings '-Xlinker -dll'
'' and '-implib:liblibtmpso.dll.a', and every Linux '-dll' died at the link.
''
'' THE LINE, NOT THE LINK. On a Windows host there is no Linux sysroot to link
'' against, so the exit code is not asserted; '-v' echoes each tool command before
'' it runs, and that is what is checked. The .so itself -- loaded by programs built
'' by fbc and by tiko, through '-l' and through dylibload -- was measured under WSL
'' (HANDOFF section 7).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -v -target linux-x86_64 -dll tests/codegen/src/export.bas -o tests/driver/libtmpso.so
'' EXPECT-OUT: -fPIC
'' EXPECT-OUT: -shared -Wl,-soname,libtmpso.so
'' EXPECT-NOT: -implib
'' EXPECT-NOT: -Xlinker -dll
